A||||4||Rocketman||What is the WS6 handling package??||||5||
Z||000000||Rocketman||02-25-2000||11:09 PM||||I saw that it was mentioned in a previous post and I have no clue what it is.  I have an 84 SE and Would like more info if anyone can provide it!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||02-25-2000||11:17 PM||||It's the handling package for the suspension.  Not to be confused with the upgraded suspension for the '88s.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rocketman||02-26-2000||07:57 AM||||Hey, that's great Monkeyman!  But what makes it different from the suspension on the regular Sport Coupe and Econo model?  And is it only on the 84, or did it come with all SE's? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||02-26-2000||11:05 AM||||WS-6 has different shocks/struts and a 28mm sway bar up front. Econo sway bar is 22mm. The '88 suspension is a different design altogether. Gennerally if the car came with the 14" aluminum rims it had the WS-6 but this is only when it was new. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||02-27-2000||12:59 PM||||WS-6 is the GM option code used for a so called performance suspension. Exactly what that means changes nearly every year, and depends on what car is involved. The WS-6 designation is used across many models.<P>You can add most, if not all, of the WS-6 improvment to any Fiero. You have to know what it came with to start. WS-6 is not the only suspension upgrade Fiero had.<P>The simple fact is current suspension parts are often far better than what WS-6 offered for Fiero. Event simple things make big improvments.<P>here are 3 simple, even cheap, items:<P>intall polyurethane sway bar bushings. This is cheap and produces the result of a stiffer bar.<P>install better shocks and struts. If yours are still OEM then they are worn out. (Unless you got lucky and found a car with only around 50,000 miles on it) Monroe, KYB, Koni, Gabriel, and others make products for Fiero.<P>Install Pollyurethane Cradle bushings. This will improve rear end stiffness without changing ride much. It can help manual transmission cars trmendously as polly will fight torque twisting of the craddle far better than rubber.||||reg||1
